    {
      "id": "conditional_hidden_flow_predictability_drift",
      "name": "Hidden-Flow Predictability Direction",
      "class_name": "",
      "description": "Compute a causal rolling entropy proxy from the empirical distribution of recent joint signed-trade and return-direction states, then form signed flow pressure from rolling trade, hidden-volume, and effective LOB-imbalance agreement. The cross-sectional signal is directional pressure multiplied by an inverse-entropy gate and reduced when quoted/effective spreads indicate that the predicted continuation is likely already fully priced.",
      "formula": "",
      "trading_idea": "The supplied paper argues that low order-flow entropy identifies informed activity and predicts future move magnitude, but its sign-invariant construction intentionally discards direction. This factor restores directional content only when low predictability is accompanied by persistent, sign-consistent hidden and visible trade flow, and when that flow agrees with effective-book imbalance. The opposite side is liquidity providers and short-horizon mean-reversion traders who treat a temporarily stable price as evidence that the imbalance is harmless; the hypothesis fails if low-entropy, directionally aligned flow does not produce materially more signed 60-bar return than equally large but high-entropy flow.",
