    {
      "id": "markov_spread_mobility_flow_projection",
      "name": "Spread-State Mobility Flow Projection",
      "class_name": "",
      "description": "For each ticker, classify the current spread as compressed, normal, or expanded relative to its causal rolling distribution and combine it with the prior spread state to form a spread-transition regime. Estimate a causal rolling expected absolute return or squared-return intensity for each regime, then multiply this mobility estimate by a signed pressure consensus from trade, orderFlow, lobImb, and effLobImb, downweighting bars with unusually high effective spread relative to quoted spread.",
      "formula": "",
      "trading_idea": "Large-tick price formation is state dependent: the probability that directional order-book pressure becomes an actual price move changes materially with the prevailing spread state and its transition history. Following the coupled return-spread dynamics in Modeling the coupled return-spread high frequency dynamics of large tick assets, buy or sell pressure should be more predictive when the current spread-transition state has historically been associated with elevated subsequent price mobility, rather than when price is pinned despite similar flow. The other side is passive liquidity providers and execution algorithms that condition on current queue conditions but underweight the persistence of the spread/return state; the hypothesis is falsified if signed pressure has equal or lower forward efficacy in high estimated mobility states than in low mobility states.",
